Next, I will determine which of these singularities are inside the contour \( C \). The contour \( C \) is a square with vertices \( \pm2 \) and \( \pm2+4i \), so it surrounds the origin.

Both singularities, \( z = 2i \) and \( z = -2i \), are inside the contour \( C \), so I will use the residue theorem to evaluate the contour integral. The residue theorem states that:

\( \oint_C f(z) dz = 2\pi i \sum \text{Res}(f, z_k) \)

where \( \text{Res}(f, z_k) \) is the residue of \( f(z) \) at the singularity \( z_k \).

I will calculate the residues for each singularity:

